Test-only fix-up (branch test/7.2.12-sam, never merged): appends to linux-surface's surface-sam patch set
(patches/7.2/0007-surface-sam.patch) the patch "platform/surface: aggregator: Defer probe while the wakeup
GPIO is unavailable", exactly as in linux-surface-wip p-h17/sam-probe-defer (65f18afb, draft PR #6).
ssam_irq_setup() uses gpiod_get_optional(), so -EPROBE_DEFER from the not-yet-bound pinctrl_tigerlake
reaches the probe instead of becoming "error -EINVAL: failed to setup IRQ". 0007-surface-sam.patch is
identical in linux-surface's fedora-43-7.2.12-1 and our 7.2.12-pro9 branch, so the diff applies to both.
No Signed-off-by yet: the owner adds his own before it goes upstream. Drop once the boot test is done.
---
diff --git a/patches/7.2/0007-surface-sam.patch b/patches/7.2/0007-surface-sam.patch
index 9177f91..a9869be 100644
--- a/patches/7.2/0007-surface-sam.patch
+++ b/patches/7.2/0007-surface-sam.patch
@@ -209,3 +209,89 @@ index d37a7e4c6..e0c07e5d8 100644
 -- 
 2.55.0
 
+From 420e76a97a5c5065da4ae88bf19c8d0a9f36762f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Chris Simpson <chris@nilk.net>
+Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:19:45 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] platform/surface: aggregator: Defer probe while the wakeup
+ GPIO is unavailable
+
+Since commit b27622f13172 ("platform/surface: Add OF support"),
+ssam_irq_setup() treats every error from gpiod_get() as "no wakeup GPIO
+described" and falls back to fwnode_irq_get(). On ACPI platforms the
+wakeup interrupt is only described as a GpioInt resource, so the fallback
+has nothing to find: on x86, acpi_irq_get() is a stub that returns
+-EINVAL, and even where it is implemented it only parses Interrupt
+resources.
+
+Among the errors turned into -EINVAL this way is -EPROBE_DEFER, which
+gpiod_get() returns when the GPIO controller providing the line has not
+been registered yet. That is easy to hit on x86 Surface devices: the
+Intel pinctrl driver (e.g. pinctrl_tigerlake for the INTC1055 controller
+of the Surface Pro 9) is usually built as a module, and nothing orders
+its loading before the Surface Serial Hub driver. When surface_aggregator
+is loaded early from the initramfs, for example by a modules-load.d entry
+or simply by udev coldplug ordering, the probe fails permanently, as
+reported for several Surface generations since v6.12:
+
+  surface_serial_hub serial0-0: SAM firmware version: 6.89.139
+  surface_serial_hub serial0-0: error -EINVAL: failed to setup IRQ
+
+and with it the whole Surface System Aggregator stack: no Type Cover,
+no battery information, no tablet mode switch, until the device is
+rebound by hand. Before b27622f13172 the deferral was propagated and the
+driver core retried the probe once the GPIO controller was there.
+
+Use gpiod_get_optional(), which returns NULL only when no GPIO is
+described (-ENOENT) and propagates every other error, including
+-EPROBE_DEFER, to the probe. Fall back to fwnode_irq_get() only in the
+NULL case, which is the device tree configuration the fallback was added
+for. The probe already reports the error with dev_err_probe(), so a
+deferral is logged at debug level only and shows up in the
+deferred-probe debugfs list.
+
+An earlier patch for the same problem [1] special-cased -EPROBE_DEFER
+in the fallback; as suggested in its review, pass every error on
+instead.
+
+Fixes: b27622f13172 ("platform/surface: Add OF support")
+Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org # 6.12+
+Closes: https://github.com/linux-surface/linux-surface/issues/2219
+Link: https://github.com/linux-surface/linux-surface/issues/1645
+Link: https://lore.kernel.org/platform-driver-x86/20261003044844.63157-1-janussss@163.com/ [1]
+Patchset: surface-sam
+---
+ drivers/platform/surface/aggregator/controller.c | 16 ++++++++++++----
+ 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/drivers/platform/surface/aggregator/controller.c b/drivers/platform/surface/aggregator/controller.c
+index 6a8430cb9..cfd640c31 100644
+--- a/drivers/platform/surface/aggregator/controller.c
++++ b/drivers/platform/surface/aggregator/controller.c
+@@ -2753,12 +2753,20 @@ int ssam_irq_setup(struct ssam_controller *ctrl)
+ 	 */
+ 	const int irqf = IRQF_ONESHOT | IRQF_TRIGGER_RISING | IRQF_NO_AUTOEN;
+ 
+-	gpiod = gpiod_get(dev, "ssam_wakeup-int", GPIOD_ASIS);
+-	if (IS_ERR(gpiod)) {
+-		irq = fwnode_irq_get(dev_fwnode(dev), 0);
+-	} else {
++	/*
++	 * Only fall back to the fwnode IRQ if no wakeup GPIO is described at
++	 * all. Any other error, in particular -EPROBE_DEFER while the GPIO
++	 * controller has not been registered yet, must reach the probe.
++	 */
++	gpiod = gpiod_get_optional(dev, "ssam_wakeup-int", GPIOD_ASIS);
++	if (IS_ERR(gpiod))
++		return PTR_ERR(gpiod);
++
++	if (gpiod) {
+ 		irq = gpiod_to_irq(gpiod);
+ 		gpiod_put(gpiod);
++	} else {
++		irq = fwnode_irq_get(dev_fwnode(dev), 0);
+ 	}
+ 
+ 	if (irq < 0)
+-- 
+2.43.0
+
